    "finalText": "Implementation complete and verified. Final structure:\n\n- **main.go** — chi router: `POST /links` (201/409/422), `GET /links/{code}` (200/404), `GET /r/{code}` (302 + atomic single increment), `GET /links` (ordered by id, `total`), all errors as JSON `{\"error\"}`; URL validation requires absolute http/https with host, codes must match `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$`\n- **store.go** — database/sql + pgx, `DATABASE_URL` from env, `ON CONFLICT` for race-safe 409s, retrying code generation\n- **cmd/migrate + migrations/** — versioned, idempotent pending-migration runner with DB wait\n- **start.sh** — builds offline (vendored deps), applies migrations, serves foreground on 0.0.0.0:8000\n- **README.md** — start instructions\n\nTested end-to-end: all status codes/bodies, 50 concurrent redirects incrementing exactly +50, concurrent duplicate creates yielding one 201/19×409, restart persistence, and offline rebuild. Test data was truncated and the server stopped so port 8000 is free for grading."
